// fixd_wq is deliberately left uncased, on blast radius rather than cost: a
// regression changes which functions --fix treats as reachable, so the worst
// outcome is a repair suggestion missed or offered spuriously, and --fix
// output is read before it is applied. Nothing wrong is emitted. That does
// not pay for a reader and the fixture it would need (../build/fill.id).
fix_wseed(int ow) {
  if(ow >= 0 && (import fixd_wm)[ow] == 0) {
    lset((import fixd_wm), ow, 1);
    push((import fixd_wq), ow);
  }
} return void;
given fix_wseed_fixture (0):() then calls lset:((import fixd_wm), 0, 1)
given fix_wseed_fixture (-1):() then calls lset:[0]

// fixd_wm seeded with one unmarked entry directly, bypassing fix_wfill's
// fnames-length loop entirely (fill.id's own comment: every fix fixture
// leaves fnames empty, so fix_wfill never grows fixd_wm) -- fix_wseed's own
// guard needs a real slot to mark, not the fnames/name-registration
// machinery that guard is agnostic to. full_env comes first so fix_winit's
// own fix_wfill has a declared (empty) fnames to read instead of trapping.
fix_wseed_fixture() {
  full_env();
  fix_winit();
  push((import fixd_wm), 0);
} return void;
